<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>DB Assistant - Oracle Select AI</title>
    <style>
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<div style="${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE}">
    <b>Oracle Autonomous Database Select AI</b><br>
</div>
Transform how you interact with your data.<br>
Oracle Select AI enables you to use natural language to query your Autonomous Database, generating SQL queries automatically to deliver fast and accurate insights about your business. <br>
Powered by advanced AI models, this feature simplifies data analysis for users of all skill levels, from business analysts to developers.

<br>
<br>
<br>
<u>Before You Begin</u><br>
(unless already provisioned by your organization)<br><br>
To use Select AI, ensure the following:
<ul>
    <li><b>Database Privileges</b> - Obtain execute privileges for the <code>DBMS_CLOUD</code> and <code>DBMS_CLOUD_AI</code> packages to enable AI-driven query generation.</li>
    <li><b>Network Access</b> - Configure network ACLs to allow connectivity to the selected AI provider’s endpoint.</li>
    <li><b>AI Provider Credentials</b> - Provide valid API credentials for a supported AI provider (OpenAI, Cohere, or Oracle Cloud Infrastructure Generative AI).</li>
    <li><b>AI Profiles</b> - Set up AI profiles to define which schemas, tables, or views are accessible for natural language queries, ensuring secure and controlled data access.</li>
</ul>
Refer to the <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/cloud/paas/autonomous-database/adbsa/select-ai.html">Oracle Select AI Documentation</a> for detailed setup instructions.

<br>
<br>
<br>
<b>Note</b><br>
Oracle Select AI is an experimental feature in preview. Results may vary based on query complexity or data model. Validate outputs and report any issues to the Oracle® Database Navigator development team for continuous improvement.
</body>
</html>
